Release 4.6.1.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 18:40:15

Fixed. The wiki chapter and the installer's own messages are checked once more against the code and the writing
standard. Three sentences in the wiki chapter are now active. They are about the paired XBOX controller, the picture
that scales to fit and the hidden IPv6 address. The installer's message after --uninstall --purge is now two
sentences. No labels are renamed. Two facts are corrected in the wiki chapter. The chapter named only On, Sleep and
Off as power states. The app also shows Updating and Unknown. The chapter said the app talks to Microsoft's XBOX
services only when you sign in, refresh, wake a console or stream. The app also refreshes by itself when it starts
signed in. The installers' shared messages and the disclaimer stay as they are. Nothing the app does has changed. No
tests changed.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 15:13:54

Release 4.6.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 14:26:18

Fixed. The app's text is rewritten to the writing standard: the wiki chapter, the README, and the window's hints,
tooltips and messages. Sentences are short, hold one fact each and no longer chain facts with a colon, a semicolon or
long parentheses. The link under the title row is labeled Wiki, no longer Manual. Messages reworded: the introduction,
the Sign in and Wake tooltips, the text beside Microsoft account, "Off. Switch it on in the XBOX's settings" in the
Remote play column, the note under the cloud games, the waking, signed-out and remote-play-is-off messages, the
games' names note, the queue's "In the queue for a cloud server. About 2 minutes to wait…", and the sign-in errors
(saved sign-in no longer accepted, code expired, no XBOX profile, child account). The README names the wiki, not the
manual. One fact corrected in the wiki's Privacy section: the log shows the last part of an IPv4 address only, and hides
an IPv6 address whole (the chapter said every network address keeps its last part). The installer's messages stay as
they are. Nothing the app does has changed. Tests changed: test_stream.py (the queue text) and test_main_window.py
("Sign in again").

